{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.math.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    private static final long MOD = 998244353L;\n    private static long[] fact;\n    \n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n        \n        int N = sc.nextInt();\n        long K = sc.nextLong();\n        \n        if (K >= N) {\n            out.println(0);\n            out.close();\n            return;\n        }\n        \n        int C = N - (int)K;\n        \n        fact = new long[200001];\n        fact[0] = 1;\n        for (int i = 1; i <= 200000; i++) {\n            fact[i] = (i * fact[i-1]) % MOD;\n        }\n        \n        long result = 0;\n        int s = 1;\n        for (int i = C; i >= 1; i--) {\n            long term = (nCr(C, i) * modExp(i, N, MOD)) % MOD;\n            result = (result + s * term + 2 * MOD) % MOD;\n            s = -s;\n        }\n        \n        long factor = (C == N) ? 1 : (2 * nCr(N, C)) % MOD;\n        out.println((result * factor) % MOD);\n        out.close();\n    }\n    \n    private static long nCr(int n, int r) {\n        long denom = (fact[r] * fact[n - r]) % MOD;\n        long inv = modExp(denom, MOD - 2, MOD);\n        return (fact[n] * inv) % MOD;\n    }\n    \n    private static long modExp(long b, long e, long m) {\n        if (e < 0) return 0;\n        long res = 1;\n        b %= m;\n        while (e > 0) {\n            if ((e & 1) == 1) res = (res * b) % m;\n            b = (b * b) % m;\n            e >>= 1;\n        }\n        return res;\n    }\n    \n    static class Scanner {\n        BufferedReader br;\n        StringTokenizer st;\n        \n        public Scanner(InputStream s) {\n            br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(s));\n        }\n        \n        public String next() {\n            while (st == null || !st.hasMoreElements()) {\n                try {\n                    st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n                } catch (IOException e) {\n                    e.printStackTrace();\n                }\n            }\n            return st.nextToken();\n        }\n        \n        public int nextInt() {\n            return Integer.parseInt(next());\n        }\n        \n        public long nextLong() {\n            return Long.parseLong(next());\n        }\n        \n        public double nextDouble() {\n            return Double.parseDouble(next());\n        }\n        \n        public String nextLine() {\n            String str = \"\";\n            try {\n                str = br.readLine();\n            } catch (IOException e) {\n                e.printStackTrace();\n            }\n            return str;\n        }\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nimport math\n\nMOD = 998244353\nfact = None\n\ndef mod_exp(b, e, m):\n    if e < 0:\n        return 0\n    res = 1\n    b %= m\n    while e > 0:\n        if (e & 1) == 1:\n            res = (res * b) % m\n        b = (b * b) % m\n        e >>= 1\n    return res\n\ndef nCr(n, r):\n    denom = (fact[r] * fact[n - r]) % MOD\n    inv = mod_exp(denom, MOD - 2, MOD)\n    return (fact[n] * inv) % MOD\n\ndef main():\n    global fact\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    sc_index = 0\n    \n    def next_int():\n        nonlocal sc_index\n        val = int(input_data[sc_index])\n        sc_index += 1\n        return val\n    \n    def next_long():\n        nonlocal sc_index\n        val = int(input_data[sc_index])\n        sc_index += 1\n        return val\n    \n    N = next_int()\n    K = next_long()\n    \n    if K >= N:\n        print(0)\n        return\n    \n    C = N - int(K)\n    \n    fact = [0] * 200001\n    fact[0] = 1\n    for i in range(1, 200001):\n        fact[i] = (i * fact[i-1]) % MOD\n    \n    result = 0\n    s = 1\n    for i in range(C, 0, -1):\n        term = (nCr(C, i) * mod_exp(i, N, MOD)) % MOD\n        result = (result + s * term + 2 * MOD) % MOD\n        s = -s\n    \n    if C == N:\n        factor = 1\n    else:\n        factor = (2 * nCr(N, C)) % MOD\n    \n    print((result * factor) % MOD)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-7.581423415103927e-05, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.00542288227006793, -0.0008424547268077731, -0.17975640296936035, -0.004699257668107748, -0.0020831567235291004, -0.00023135847004596144, -0.00023707917716819793, 0.0, -4.768370445162873e-07, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -2.145764938177308e-06, -2.074220174108632e-05, -0.02079739421606064, -3.576272320060525e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.4740888476371765, -0.0003300360403954983, -1.1920858014491387e-05, -0.4862128496170044, -3.611976353568025e-05, -3.576214658096433e-05, -0.02949777990579605, -0.12882380187511444, -0.006718901451677084, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -1.07288